<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell mid-April Bombay naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell mid-April Bombay naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting mid-April from Bombay on the west coast, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on April 3 and is valid until April 4.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN cargo from Bombay lifting February 20-22 was awarded at $23.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
